1
00:01:00,875 --> 00:01:02,250
-Morning, Madhavi.
-Good morning, Madhavi.

2
00:01:02,333 --> 00:01:05,250
Good morning.
What's the matter? It's Sunday!

3
00:01:06,208 --> 00:01:07,541
Yeah.

4
00:01:07,625 --> 00:01:08,750
What happened?

5
00:01:09,458 --> 00:01:10,916
We have to head to Srinagar.

6
00:01:11,541 --> 00:01:12,708
Pack your bags.

7
00:01:13,291 --> 00:01:16,000
Sangy is flying Mirages now
and Chou sir is on leave,

8
00:01:16,083 --> 00:01:17,375
so we all have to go.

9
00:01:17,458 --> 00:01:19,166
-Okay.
-See you, Madhavi.

10
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:20,250
See you, Madhavi.

11
00:01:25,583 --> 00:01:30,833
Last night in the Kargil sector, a major
ammunition depot of the Indian Army

12
00:01:30,916 --> 00:01:34,666
was bombed to smithereens
by unknown intruders.

13
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:38,750
And today, the Kargil magistrate's house
has also been targeted.

14
00:01:38,833 --> 00:01:42,416
Tololing Complex, located amongst
the treacherous peaks of Kargil sector,

15
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:46,583
and located closest
to the Srinagar-Leh Highway,

16
00:01:46,666 --> 00:01:48,750
has witnessed constant firing.

17
00:01:48,833 --> 00:01:51,500
-Shortage of ammunition and supplies has…
-Sir.

18
00:01:52,708 --> 00:01:54,875
The ISI chief has called three times.

19
00:01:55,541 --> 00:01:56,791
What should we do?

20
00:01:56,875 --> 00:01:58,208
Indian DGMO?

21
00:01:59,125 --> 00:02:01,333
Sir, I've already lied to the Indian DGMO.

22
00:02:02,083 --> 00:02:04,416
But we'll have to tell
the ISI chief the truth.

23
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:07,041
No need, General.

24
00:02:08,458 --> 00:02:11,250
Didn't the chief show Mian sahib
the captured posts from Skardu?

25
00:02:11,333 --> 00:02:13,916
Yes, but he doesn't know
they're on the other side of the LoC.

26
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,083
Yes. But that's exactly our plan.

27
00:02:16,791 --> 00:02:19,458
Sir, before Mian sahib
hears it from someone else--

28
00:02:23,625 --> 00:02:25,625
Organize a briefing.

29
00:02:28,041 --> 00:02:31,625
The time has come
for the prime minister to play his part.

30
00:03:27,791 --> 00:03:29,041
Sardar, do you remember

31
00:03:29,833 --> 00:03:31,958
when we were newly married?

32
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:34,625
I was in the habit of waking up late.

33
00:03:35,916 --> 00:03:38,000
And you flew your MiG

34
00:03:38,083 --> 00:03:41,000
over our house
every morning to wake me up.

35
00:03:42,875 --> 00:03:46,500
If you don't want me to get back
into the habit of waking up late again,

36
00:03:47,375 --> 00:03:49,041
come back to wake me up.

37
00:04:08,208 --> 00:04:09,625
Can't you stay still?

38
00:04:11,458 --> 00:04:13,000
It'll just take two minutes.

39
00:04:13,083 --> 00:04:15,750
I have to finish packing.
Do we have to do this now?

40
00:04:15,833 --> 00:04:17,750
Then when? Your birthday is coming up.

41
00:04:18,291 --> 00:04:21,208
It's just a small mission.
I'll be back before my birthday.

42
00:04:24,750 --> 00:04:25,875
Don't you worry.

43
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:29,666
I am not worrying. Turn.

44
00:06:23,625 --> 00:06:25,625
Welcome to GHQ, Mian sahib.

45
00:06:27,791 --> 00:06:30,166
I don't understand
the purpose of this urgent meeting.

46
00:06:31,250 --> 00:06:32,625
Come, Mian sahib.

47
00:06:32,708 --> 00:06:33,791
Let's sit down and discuss.

48
00:06:33,875 --> 00:06:34,708
Shall we?

49
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:38,833
Tell me,

50
00:06:39,708 --> 00:06:41,750
what do you want to brief me on?

51
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:47,583
Sir,

52
00:06:48,125 --> 00:06:50,500
as per your wish, our freedom fighters

53
00:06:50,583 --> 00:06:52,791
braving the harsh winter,

54
00:06:52,875 --> 00:06:55,375
have occupied many new peaks
in the valley.

55
00:06:57,416 --> 00:07:00,000
Some of those posts are across LoC.

56
00:07:04,041 --> 00:07:06,833
Sir, these are the posts overlooking NH1

57
00:07:06,916 --> 00:07:09,416
that Chief showed you in Skardu.

58
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:11,333
As Chief had briefed you--

59
00:07:11,416 --> 00:07:15,750
General Musharraf, has the Army forgotten
how to answer direct questions?

60
00:07:30,166 --> 00:07:32,000
This is the LoC, sir.

61
00:07:33,291 --> 00:07:35,791
Every single captured post

62
00:07:36,625 --> 00:07:38,166
across the LoC

63
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:40,791
are Indian posts.

64
00:07:44,041 --> 00:07:45,041
Good morning, gentlemen.

65
00:07:45,875 --> 00:07:48,916
You have all been summoned here
at extremely short notice.

66
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:52,583
Because the Kargil, Drass,
and Batalik sectors

67
00:07:52,666 --> 00:07:55,375
are seeing heavy attacks on our army.

68
00:07:55,458 --> 00:07:59,583
And it seems like
a highly coordinated attack.

69
00:07:59,666 --> 00:08:01,416
-Oak.
-Sir.

70
00:08:02,208 --> 00:08:04,583
The army's ammunition dump
has been blown up.

71
00:08:05,083 --> 00:08:07,791
Their recce helicopters
have also been heavily damaged.

72
00:08:07,875 --> 00:08:12,041
National Highway 1,
connecting Srinagar and Leh-Ladakh

73
00:08:12,125 --> 00:08:14,000
has been completely cut off.

74
00:08:14,083 --> 00:08:15,833
Army supplies are getting affected.

75
00:08:15,916 --> 00:08:18,083
Now, for those unfamiliar
with this terrain.

76
00:08:18,833 --> 00:08:22,875
This stretch of Drass, Kargil, and Batalik

77
00:08:22,958 --> 00:08:25,583
is a 115 kilometer stretch.

78
00:08:25,666 --> 00:08:27,916
Right now,
it is a black hole for the army.

79
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,250
Quite frankly,

80
00:08:29,333 --> 00:08:30,750
it is for us too.

81
00:08:32,375 --> 00:08:37,416
And so, air combat
and bombing squadrons will be on standby,

82
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:40,083
until Golden Arrows find the answer

83
00:08:40,166 --> 00:08:42,583
to the most fundamental question…

84
00:08:44,125 --> 00:08:46,083
Who are we fighting?

85
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,041
Then why not be clear about it?

86
00:08:50,125 --> 00:08:52,833
That these aren't Mujahideen,
but the Pakistani Army.

87
00:08:52,916 --> 00:08:55,125
As far as I can remember,

88
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:58,000
you never made this clear
to Mian sahib in Skardu.

89
00:08:58,083 --> 00:09:00,833
For the world and India,
technically, they are Mujahideen.

90
00:09:00,916 --> 00:09:03,291
-Everyone has been trained in Pashto.
-Pashto?

91
00:09:03,916 --> 00:09:06,875
What if they're trained in Pashto?
What if they get caught?

92
00:09:06,958 --> 00:09:09,000
They'll only get caught

93
00:09:09,583 --> 00:09:12,333
when the Indians reach that height.

94
00:09:12,416 --> 00:09:15,708
Just as we couldn't reach them in Siachen,
this time they won't--

95
00:09:15,791 --> 00:09:16,666
Enough!

96
00:09:16,750 --> 00:09:18,416
Enough of this briefing!

97
00:09:20,458 --> 00:09:23,916
You'll stop this reckless operation that
was undertaken without my knowledge.

98
00:09:25,416 --> 00:09:26,958
Wait for my further orders.

99
00:09:31,041 --> 00:09:31,875
Let's go.

100
00:09:33,125 --> 00:09:34,125
Mian sahib…

101
00:09:35,375 --> 00:09:37,375
Gandhi, Patel,

102
00:09:38,125 --> 00:09:39,500
Nehru,

103
00:09:39,583 --> 00:09:40,666
Mountbatten,

104
00:09:41,875 --> 00:09:44,958
none of them
wanted Pakistan to be created.

105
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,041
But the Great Leader remained adamant.

106
00:09:48,958 --> 00:09:53,416
There are only a few leaders in the world
who have changed the world map.

107
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:58,625
And even fewer who have given birth
to a new nation.

108
00:09:59,625 --> 00:10:01,541
If Pakistan exists today,

109
00:10:01,625 --> 00:10:04,166
it is because of Muhammad Ali Jinnah.

110
00:10:06,666 --> 00:10:10,416
We have snatched
a big chunk of Kashmir from India.

111
00:10:11,333 --> 00:10:13,541
And if we remain adamant this time,

112
00:10:15,375 --> 00:10:16,750
then like the Great Leader,

113
00:10:16,833 --> 00:10:19,291
you will change
the map of this world, sir.

114
00:10:19,375 --> 00:10:22,125
General sahib, I came here
for a military briefing.

115
00:10:23,458 --> 00:10:25,458
Not for advice on political matters.

116
00:10:29,875 --> 00:10:31,791
I told you, Pervez sahib,

117
00:10:33,208 --> 00:10:35,041
no more surprises.

118
00:10:36,791 --> 00:10:40,708
But you seem to have forgotten that
you're the Army Chief of this country,

119
00:10:41,333 --> 00:10:42,500
not the Prime Minister.

120
00:10:47,958 --> 00:10:48,958
Remember that going forward.

121
00:10:50,041 --> 00:10:51,125
Let's go.

122
00:10:55,791 --> 00:10:58,000
Such a huge operation

123
00:10:58,083 --> 00:11:00,375
and none of us got a whiff of it?

124
00:11:01,458 --> 00:11:04,541
So… what's the plan going forward?

125
00:11:07,583 --> 00:11:08,666
What's the plan?

126
00:11:09,291 --> 00:11:12,458
Now we have to find
a new army chief, Abba ji.

127
00:11:13,208 --> 00:11:16,083
Have you seen his audacity?
Without asking me,

128
00:11:16,166 --> 00:11:18,791
without the Prime Minister's permission,

129
00:11:19,541 --> 00:11:20,833
he has pulled this stunt.

130
00:11:20,916 --> 00:11:23,916
Is this the right time
to remove General Musharraf?

131
00:11:25,958 --> 00:11:26,791
What…

132
00:11:27,375 --> 00:11:28,875
What are you saying, Abba ji?

133
00:11:28,958 --> 00:11:30,500
Are you even listening?

134
00:11:49,875 --> 00:11:51,208
I told you,

135
00:11:52,375 --> 00:11:55,125
running a country
is like running a business.

136
00:11:56,333 --> 00:12:01,708
And to remain in the business of politics,
you have to be on the winning side.

137
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:05,375
A victory you couldn't achieve
during the peace talks…

138
00:12:05,458 --> 00:12:09,791
if Musharraf manages to achieve it
without you,

139
00:12:11,250 --> 00:12:13,208
where will you be left standing?

140
00:12:13,791 --> 00:12:16,416
Which is why, if he's winning the war,

141
00:12:18,125 --> 00:12:20,541
this operation should be the PM's.

142
00:12:24,416 --> 00:12:25,625
Yours.

143
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:29,541
If you prove worthy of this moment,

144
00:12:29,625 --> 00:12:33,958
history will truly place you
alongside Jinnah sahib.

145
00:12:35,125 --> 00:12:39,291
Reconvene the Cabinet this evening.
Call General Musharraf too.

146
00:12:48,125 --> 00:12:49,083
Boys,

147
00:12:49,166 --> 00:12:50,958
we are the eyes of the nation now.

148
00:12:52,791 --> 00:12:56,333
-And that's a huge responsibility.
-And a very difficult one too.

149
00:12:57,166 --> 00:12:59,916
One thousand to two thousand feet.

150
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,250
As a low-altitude photo-recce squadron,

151
00:13:02,333 --> 00:13:05,375
we're trained to take photos
from these heights.

152
00:13:05,458 --> 00:13:07,625
Now, the enemy is sitting here…

153
00:13:09,333 --> 00:13:10,916
at 18,000 feet.

154
00:13:12,666 --> 00:13:14,416
Temperature, minus 25 degrees,

155
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:16,583
wind speed, 100 kilometers per hour.

156
00:13:17,541 --> 00:13:20,791
So we have to get here to take the photo.

157
00:13:20,875 --> 00:13:22,708
Twenty thousand feet.

158
00:13:22,791 --> 00:13:24,333
We know very well that

159
00:13:24,416 --> 00:13:27,416
our MiGs aren't designed
for these heights or conditions.

160
00:13:28,416 --> 00:13:30,958
Unfortunately, they know this
well enough too.

161
00:13:32,291 --> 00:13:33,958
To conceal our approach,

162
00:13:34,041 --> 00:13:36,041
we will fly through the valley

163
00:13:36,125 --> 00:13:38,166
and approach the target sector,

164
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:41,458
then climb without warning

165
00:13:42,791 --> 00:13:44,916
and fly over the enemy sector.

166
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,041
There are mountains on both sides.

167
00:13:47,125 --> 00:13:48,416
A minor slip,

168
00:13:50,291 --> 00:13:51,250
and you will crash.

169
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:56,333
Ahuja and I will fly the first sortie.

170
00:13:58,916 --> 00:14:00,708
Will one sortie be enough?

171
00:14:01,625 --> 00:14:04,166
Will we be able to capture
their exact locations?

172
00:14:04,833 --> 00:14:06,166
Even I don't know this.

173
00:14:06,250 --> 00:14:09,625
All we know is that in the history
of the Indian Air Force,

174
00:14:09,708 --> 00:14:12,708
no photo-recce squadron
has ever played such a critical role.

175
00:14:13,375 --> 00:14:15,000
We're the select chosen few

176
00:14:15,750 --> 00:14:18,666
who've been given the opportunity
to protect our borders.

177
00:14:20,750 --> 00:14:23,375
Golden Arrows, are we ready?

178
00:14:23,458 --> 00:14:24,333
Yes, sir.

179
00:14:24,416 --> 00:14:25,708
-Are we ready?
-Yes, sir.

180
00:14:25,791 --> 00:14:27,291
-Are we ready?
-Yes, sir!

181
00:14:31,625 --> 00:14:33,166
Plans for tomorrow?

182
00:14:33,250 --> 00:14:34,458
Depends, sir.

183
00:14:34,541 --> 00:14:36,333
Let's see how today's recce goes.

184
00:14:36,416 --> 00:14:39,291
Ideally, we should do
multiple sorties with the boys.

185
00:14:41,208 --> 00:14:42,916
I'm talking about your birthday.

186
00:14:43,791 --> 00:14:45,416
Birthday plans at a time like this, sir?

187
00:14:46,416 --> 00:14:48,875
In any case, one ends up
with over 100 birthdays in a year.

188
00:14:49,583 --> 00:14:52,666
Celebrating just one day
would be undervaluing oneself, right?

189
00:14:55,458 --> 00:14:57,250
Isn't every successful landing
a birthday, sir?

190
00:14:58,416 --> 00:15:00,083
Your twisted logic on this too.

191
00:15:00,166 --> 00:15:02,625
The whole world runs
on twisted logic, sir.

192
00:15:03,625 --> 00:15:06,458
Otherwise, who'd fight
for these barren mountains?

193
00:15:06,541 --> 00:15:07,791
See you on the other side.

194
00:15:08,541 --> 00:15:09,541
Will do, sir.

195
00:15:32,583 --> 00:15:33,833
Setting course for IP.

196
00:15:33,916 --> 00:15:35,000
Roger, sir.

197
00:15:48,666 --> 00:15:50,416
Arrow 2, careful.

198
00:15:51,041 --> 00:15:52,166
We're in the valley now.

199
00:15:52,250 --> 00:15:53,500
Roger, on your tail.

200
00:15:55,708 --> 00:15:58,000
Arrow 1, strong cross winds

201
00:15:58,083 --> 00:16:00,125
are pushing you to the right.
Abort valley approach, Arrow 1.

202
00:16:00,208 --> 00:16:02,000
Arrow 2, we'll have to fight it.

203
00:16:02,083 --> 00:16:04,250
Arrow 1, we might crash into the mountain.

204
00:16:04,333 --> 00:16:05,500
It's too late, Arrow 2.

205
00:16:05,583 --> 00:16:06,833
Start crabbing now!

206
00:16:11,791 --> 00:16:14,916
Maintaining RPM and altitude,
keep nosing up.

207
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,583
Maintaining, Arrow 1.

208
00:16:23,833 --> 00:16:25,791
Arrow 2, stand by for left exit.

209
00:16:25,875 --> 00:16:26,791
Roger.

210
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:34,166
Be ready to exit the valley.

211
00:16:34,250 --> 00:16:35,625
Mindful on your left!

212
00:16:35,708 --> 00:16:37,416
Exit valley now!

213
00:16:45,458 --> 00:16:47,166
That was close, Arrow 2.

214
00:16:47,250 --> 00:16:50,625
This will be tough for the boys.
We need a plan B for the valley approach.

215
00:16:50,708 --> 00:16:51,750
Strongly agree, Arrow 1.

216
00:16:58,208 --> 00:17:01,583
Arrow 2, banking left 45 degrees
for better visual.

217
00:17:01,666 --> 00:17:02,500
Roger.

218
00:17:02,583 --> 00:17:04,583
I'll bank 45 degrees and see, sir.

219
00:17:10,041 --> 00:17:12,083
Come on, everyone, in the sangar. Quick!

220
00:17:12,166 --> 00:17:15,125
Cover it. Everybody, hide. Move it!

221
00:17:54,208 --> 00:17:56,666
All I can see is snow everywhere.

222
00:17:57,833 --> 00:18:01,083
Arrow 1, I think I've spotted something.
Marking coordinates for you.

223
00:18:01,166 --> 00:18:02,916
What are you suggesting, Arrow 2?

224
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,541
I feel, we should take another pass.
A little lower.

225
00:18:06,541 --> 00:18:08,791
All right. Fuel check?

226
00:18:09,666 --> 00:18:11,541
Joker plus hundred. Plenty of fuel.

227
00:18:11,625 --> 00:18:13,166
Exercise caution, Arrow 2.

228
00:18:13,250 --> 00:18:15,000
Hostile fire possible.

229
00:18:21,833 --> 00:18:23,416
The jets are coming back.

230
00:18:27,458 --> 00:18:29,500
Approaching target. Turn on cameras.

231
00:18:29,583 --> 00:18:30,958
Cameras on standby.

232
00:18:37,041 --> 00:18:41,750
Target in five, four, three, two, one.

233
00:18:41,833 --> 00:18:43,166
-Cameras on.
-Cameras on.

234
00:18:55,250 --> 00:18:57,791
Arrow 2, did you spot anything
during the second pass?

235
00:18:57,875 --> 00:18:59,875
-I did see something.
-What?

236
00:18:59,958 --> 00:19:01,333
Not sure, sir.

237
00:19:01,833 --> 00:19:03,166
But there's something.

238
00:19:04,250 --> 00:19:05,583
Let's see.

239
00:19:35,416 --> 00:19:36,416
I'll take it.

240
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:38,291
You guys get Tony's reel.

241
00:19:38,375 --> 00:19:40,375
-Sir, I can do that--
-Didn't I tell you?

242
00:19:40,458 --> 00:19:42,833
Take the reel
from Tony sir's jet and go to PIC.

243
00:19:43,916 --> 00:19:46,083
I need these reels developed by evening.

244
00:19:56,916 --> 00:19:58,041
Good evening, Mian sahib.

245
00:19:59,958 --> 00:20:02,208
I conducted myself wrongly with you.

246
00:20:04,625 --> 00:20:05,458
I'm sorry.

247
00:20:05,541 --> 00:20:07,708
Don't say that, Mian sahib.

248
00:20:08,291 --> 00:20:09,750
Your anger is justified.

249
00:20:10,625 --> 00:20:14,500
But our goal was to keep you
all insulated till the right time came.

250
00:20:14,583 --> 00:20:15,458
General,

251
00:20:16,083 --> 00:20:18,833
the way you kept the operation secret

252
00:20:19,833 --> 00:20:21,541
is highly commendable.

253
00:20:21,625 --> 00:20:25,125
Operation Mountaineering.
That's the name of the operation.

254
00:20:25,208 --> 00:20:27,541
And now Mountaineering
is our responsibility too.

255
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:31,875
-You just said it.
-Absolutely, Mian sahib.

256
00:20:31,958 --> 00:20:34,625
Our men have done their job.

257
00:20:35,125 --> 00:20:40,291
Now all of you have to leverage
this situation diplomatically.

258
00:20:40,375 --> 00:20:41,416
Sartaj sahib.

259
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:42,416
Sir?

260
00:20:43,291 --> 00:20:46,375
What's the international reaction
to this issue?

261
00:20:46,458 --> 00:20:49,583
Sir, Indians are leaning towards
Russian support.

262
00:20:50,166 --> 00:20:51,000
And the US?

263
00:20:52,666 --> 00:20:56,416
America, as expected, is neutral for now.

264
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:59,750
I think, we should talk to China.

265
00:20:59,833 --> 00:21:01,458
If we get China's support,

266
00:21:01,541 --> 00:21:04,000
India will be cornered
not just militarily,

267
00:21:04,083 --> 00:21:06,041
but on the diplomatic front too.

268
00:21:06,125 --> 00:21:07,125
That works too.

269
00:21:07,208 --> 00:21:09,833
Then the ISI chief
and I will talk to Beijing.

270
00:21:09,916 --> 00:21:11,208
Nawaz,

271
00:21:11,291 --> 00:21:13,083
I think

272
00:21:13,166 --> 00:21:15,750
General Musharraf should go to China.

273
00:21:15,833 --> 00:21:19,000
To open a channel with a military state,

274
00:21:19,083 --> 00:21:21,583
who better than the Army Chief?

275
00:21:31,708 --> 00:21:32,708
Jai Hind, sir.

276
00:21:34,458 --> 00:21:35,750
Jai Hind. Yes, Patil?

277
00:21:35,833 --> 00:21:38,541
-It's an emergency.
-What kind of emergency?

278
00:21:38,625 --> 00:21:40,750
I don't know, sir.
Tony sir is calling you.

279
00:21:52,916 --> 00:21:56,500
He is a jolly good fellow
He is a jolly good fellow

280
00:21:57,125 --> 00:21:59,958
He is a jolly good fellow

281
00:22:00,541 --> 00:22:02,625
And so say all of us

282
00:22:05,791 --> 00:22:08,375
-Ahuja, happy birthday.
-Sir!

283
00:22:10,625 --> 00:22:12,375
-Happy birthday.
-Thank you, sir.

284
00:22:12,458 --> 00:22:16,041
Happy birthday, dear Ahuja sir

285
00:22:16,125 --> 00:22:19,500
Happy birthday to you

286
00:22:19,583 --> 00:22:22,291
Alka ma'am loves you

287
00:22:22,375 --> 00:22:23,208
Good one.

288
00:22:23,291 --> 00:22:26,000
We all love you…

289
00:22:26,708 --> 00:22:27,791
Flying officer Dhaliwal.

290
00:22:30,333 --> 00:22:32,041
Happy birthday to you

291
00:22:32,125 --> 00:22:35,500
Okay, I will. Hold on.
Sir, the pictures are ready.

292
00:22:49,333 --> 00:22:50,250
Here…

293
00:22:59,458 --> 00:23:01,333
Project this negative.

294
00:23:23,500 --> 00:23:24,416
This.

295
00:23:25,916 --> 00:23:27,166
Just this area.

296
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:30,041
Get me a printout of this.

297
00:23:31,041 --> 00:23:32,000
Excuse me, sir.

298
00:23:36,666 --> 00:23:39,333
Sir, these are enlargements
of our recce photos.

299
00:23:40,541 --> 00:23:42,291
If you look at these magnified images,

300
00:23:43,125 --> 00:23:45,333
footsteps are clearly visible on the snow.

301
00:23:46,541 --> 00:23:48,291
But these footprints aren't random.

302
00:23:48,375 --> 00:23:50,666
They're a single coordinated trail.

303
00:23:51,333 --> 00:23:53,500
Mujahideen don't move in single file.

304
00:23:54,750 --> 00:23:56,541
It's the army that moves in single file.

305
00:23:56,625 --> 00:23:59,708
Sir, why would Mujahideen move
in such a regimental manner,

306
00:23:59,791 --> 00:24:02,375
that too in such harsh snowy conditions?

307
00:24:02,458 --> 00:24:07,125
They can walk across
any unguarded place as they like.

308
00:24:07,208 --> 00:24:08,708
I agree with the Air Chief.

309
00:24:08,791 --> 00:24:11,333
This looks to be
the Pakistan Army's doing.

310
00:24:11,416 --> 00:24:13,625
R&amp;AW has intercepted radio calls.

311
00:24:14,666 --> 00:24:16,916
They are speaking in Pashto,

312
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:22,083
but discussing army protocols.

313
00:24:22,916 --> 00:24:25,791
If we analyze the depth of this trail,

314
00:24:26,375 --> 00:24:29,416
it's clear that this trail
was not used just once.

315
00:24:29,500 --> 00:24:31,291
It's been used repeatedly.

316
00:24:31,375 --> 00:24:34,083
This means they've been sitting

317
00:24:34,166 --> 00:24:36,333
on our peaks for quite some time,

318
00:24:36,416 --> 00:24:37,375
building bases.

319
00:24:37,458 --> 00:24:39,166
Historically, sir,

320
00:24:39,250 --> 00:24:41,583
Mujahideen cross the LoC

321
00:24:41,666 --> 00:24:43,083
and carry out small attacks.

322
00:24:43,166 --> 00:24:46,208
Why would they build bases on peaks?

323
00:24:48,708 --> 00:24:49,625
Gentlemen,

324
00:24:50,583 --> 00:24:51,791
I believe

325
00:24:52,500 --> 00:24:57,166
we are faced with a limited invasion
by the Pakistani Army.

326
00:24:57,875 --> 00:24:59,708
This is not just deceit,

327
00:25:01,083 --> 00:25:04,458
but a betrayal of our trust by Pakistan.

328
00:25:06,041 --> 00:25:06,958
And we

329
00:25:07,625 --> 00:25:10,083
will respond to this betrayal.

330
00:25:12,083 --> 00:25:13,166
I…

331
00:25:15,083 --> 00:25:17,208
give permission to the Indian Air Force

332
00:25:17,291 --> 00:25:19,458
to commence bombing.

333
00:25:19,541 --> 00:25:20,708
Sir.

334
00:25:20,791 --> 00:25:21,791
But

335
00:25:22,750 --> 00:25:23,750
on one condition.

336
00:25:25,208 --> 00:25:29,250
We have to respect the Line of Control.

337
00:25:32,333 --> 00:25:33,916
Because they want us

338
00:25:34,875 --> 00:25:37,083
to cross the border,

339
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:41,166
so that they can tell the world…

340
00:25:43,166 --> 00:25:45,541
"We didn't do anything in Kargil,

341
00:25:46,375 --> 00:25:48,625
but India is crossing the border."

342
00:25:48,708 --> 00:25:51,458
Then due to the fear
of nuclear escalation,

343
00:25:52,708 --> 00:25:54,250
UK, France,

344
00:25:54,333 --> 00:25:55,916
US, Russia,

345
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:59,250
the entire international community
will pressure us into a ceasefire.

346
00:25:59,333 --> 00:26:03,791
And where everyone is positioned right now
will become the new de-facto LoC.

347
00:26:03,875 --> 00:26:05,333
This ploy of theirs

348
00:26:06,083 --> 00:26:08,375
is the biggest challenge of this war.

349
00:26:16,333 --> 00:26:19,916
We cannot cross the LoC and strike,

350
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:21,416
or we cannot cross the LoC at all?

351
00:26:22,083 --> 00:26:23,083
Both.

352
00:26:24,500 --> 00:26:28,875
We can only attack from our side,
on the captured peaks.

353
00:26:29,833 --> 00:26:30,958
But, Chief,

354
00:26:31,916 --> 00:26:34,875
the basic principle
for any air force in the world

355
00:26:34,958 --> 00:26:36,416
is to go across the line

356
00:26:36,500 --> 00:26:39,750
and neutralize enemy infrastructure.

357
00:26:39,833 --> 00:26:44,041
How will our fighters find targets
in this white ocean, sir?

358
00:26:44,125 --> 00:26:45,125
I don't know.

359
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:48,583
I just know
that if we don't do anything now,

360
00:26:48,666 --> 00:26:51,791
all that'll be left of our ground forces

361
00:26:51,875 --> 00:26:54,583
out there in the snow
will be corpses. Corpses.

362
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:06,333
Operation Safed Sagar.

363
00:27:18,541 --> 00:27:22,125
The prime minister
has authorized air strikes in this war.

364
00:27:22,208 --> 00:27:23,083
We're ready, sir.

365
00:27:23,958 --> 00:27:26,041
We've marked their supply routes.

366
00:27:26,125 --> 00:27:28,291
Marked their forward bases too.

367
00:27:28,375 --> 00:27:30,791
We'll cross the LoC tomorrow morning
and start bombing.

368
00:27:30,875 --> 00:27:33,500
But we know that
as soon as we cross the LoC,

369
00:27:33,583 --> 00:27:35,458
their F-16s may get airborne.

370
00:27:35,541 --> 00:27:37,083
So our MiG-29s--

371
00:27:39,333 --> 00:27:42,166
Their F-16s will not get airborne.

372
00:27:44,208 --> 00:27:45,500
Because we…

373
00:27:48,125 --> 00:27:49,708
will not cross the LoC.

374
00:27:53,833 --> 00:27:58,041
Sir, it's almost impossible
to hit such small camouflaged targets

375
00:27:58,125 --> 00:27:59,458
at these heights.

376
00:28:00,291 --> 00:28:02,250
No air force in the world
has ever done this.

377
00:28:02,333 --> 00:28:06,041
So? The Indian Air Force
will be the first.

378
00:28:06,708 --> 00:28:10,500
Because if we cross the LoC,
the conflict will escalate.

379
00:28:10,583 --> 00:28:13,541
Pakistan will demand a ceasefire
at international forums.

380
00:28:14,333 --> 00:28:17,166
And where the intruders
are currently positioned,

381
00:28:17,250 --> 00:28:19,166
that will de-facto become the new LoC.

382
00:28:19,833 --> 00:28:21,708
And we'll lose our land.

383
00:28:21,791 --> 00:28:23,166
We must understand

384
00:28:23,250 --> 00:28:27,958
that this is also a diplomatic war now.

385
00:28:31,541 --> 00:28:35,458
I know. I'm asking you
to strike with your hands tied.

386
00:28:36,166 --> 00:28:38,500
The Army has started Operation Vijay.

387
00:28:38,583 --> 00:28:41,083
Now, either we support them

388
00:28:42,416 --> 00:28:47,083
or sit at home
and watch their losses telecast live.

389
00:28:53,375 --> 00:28:54,625
So, gentlemen,

390
00:28:55,583 --> 00:28:57,958
is the Indian Air Force
ready for this war?

391
00:28:58,041 --> 00:28:59,583
Yes, sir!

392
00:28:59,666 --> 00:29:04,625
Operation Safed Sagar
starts tomorrow at 0700 hours.

393
00:29:08,083 --> 00:29:11,875
The ongoing Kargil conflict between India
and Pakistan has taken a new turn.

394
00:29:11,958 --> 00:29:16,291
Home Minister Lal Krishna Advani,
speaking to reporters, said…

395
00:29:16,375 --> 00:29:18,708
They have violated the Simla Agreement,

396
00:29:18,791 --> 00:29:20,750
violated the Lahore Declaration.

397
00:29:20,833 --> 00:29:23,541
Mercenaries who have been
sent across the border,

398
00:29:23,625 --> 00:29:27,291
but it is Pakistani regulars.
Pakistan Army Regulars.

399
00:29:27,375 --> 00:29:29,375
Soon after, a massive deployment

400
00:29:29,458 --> 00:29:31,750
of the Indian Army was seen
in the Drass and Kargil sectors.

401
00:29:31,833 --> 00:29:35,083
And for the first time in history,
two nuclear armed nations

402
00:29:35,166 --> 00:29:37,750
appear to be heading towards
a direct confrontation.

403
00:29:37,833 --> 00:29:39,250
Addressing the nation today,

404
00:29:39,333 --> 00:29:41,833
Indian Prime Minister Vajpayee
had this to say…

405
00:29:41,916 --> 00:29:44,666
The world has seen that we want peace.

406
00:29:44,750 --> 00:29:46,125
And now the world will see

407
00:29:46,208 --> 00:29:50,458
that to protect this peace,
we can also demonstrate our strength.

408
00:29:56,875 --> 00:29:58,083
Vajpayee sahib,

409
00:29:58,166 --> 00:30:01,541
this is not the Pakistan Army,
these are Mujahideen.

410
00:30:01,625 --> 00:30:04,125
Before making an announcement
to the international media,

411
00:30:04,208 --> 00:30:06,291
you could have at least spoken to me once?

412
00:30:08,041 --> 00:30:11,750
Sir, our government has no power
over these Mujahideen.

413
00:30:14,958 --> 00:30:15,958
Mian sahib,

414
00:30:17,416 --> 00:30:20,083
power is the very definition
of government.

415
00:30:20,875 --> 00:30:23,791
A government that has no power

416
00:30:24,458 --> 00:30:26,458
is not a government at all.

417
00:30:27,166 --> 00:30:30,666
Mian sahib, with our joint efforts,

418
00:30:30,750 --> 00:30:33,458
a new hope had arisen

419
00:30:34,625 --> 00:30:36,250
among people of both countries.

420
00:30:37,166 --> 00:30:40,958
Remember, Mian sahib, both countries

421
00:30:41,708 --> 00:30:42,791
will never

422
00:30:43,750 --> 00:30:46,291
be able to recover from this treachery.

423
00:30:56,375 --> 00:30:58,208
-Arrows?
-Arrows.

424
00:30:58,291 --> 00:30:59,416
-Sir.
-Sir.

425
00:31:04,375 --> 00:31:05,958
You couldn't sleep either, sir?

426
00:31:08,625 --> 00:31:09,875
This is my first war too.

427
00:31:11,208 --> 00:31:13,458
But nothing comes of studying
the night before an exam.

428
00:31:13,541 --> 00:31:15,625
Shall we do something else?

429
00:31:17,333 --> 00:31:18,166
At ease, boys.

430
00:31:21,458 --> 00:31:23,625
Two Truths and a Lie.

431
00:31:25,666 --> 00:31:27,791
-Ever played it?
-No, sir.

432
00:31:29,166 --> 00:31:33,083
Everyone gets to tell two truths
and one lie about themselves.

433
00:31:34,666 --> 00:31:36,958
And everyone else has to deduce

434
00:31:37,041 --> 00:31:38,791
which one is the lie.

435
00:31:38,875 --> 00:31:41,208
-Sounds like your game, sir.
-Correct.

436
00:31:42,833 --> 00:31:43,833
So I'll go first?

437
00:31:46,916 --> 00:31:49,083
I always wanted to join the Air Force.

438
00:31:50,583 --> 00:31:53,250
I said yes to marrying Alka

439
00:31:53,750 --> 00:31:57,083
when she made me
a great cup of coffee in under a minute.

440
00:31:58,416 --> 00:32:01,916
Tony. Tony hated me
the first time he met me.

441
00:32:03,291 --> 00:32:04,916
-Easy.
-This is easy, sir.

442
00:32:05,500 --> 00:32:06,625
Start guessing.

443
00:32:06,708 --> 00:32:08,666
The Tony sir thing is a lie. I'm sure.

444
00:32:08,750 --> 00:32:10,625
What Tony sir?
The Alka ma'am thing is a lie.

445
00:32:10,708 --> 00:32:11,875
No, he can't hate him.

446
00:32:11,958 --> 00:32:13,916
-Who can make coffee in a minute?
-Last option.

447
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:17,208
One can't agree to marriage on a cup
of coffee. Obviously, it's Alka ma'am.

448
00:32:17,291 --> 00:32:18,458
It looks like Tony sir to me.

449
00:32:18,541 --> 00:32:19,916
-Yes, Tony sir.
-Tony sir.

450
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:21,500
-Baldy said it.
-Time's up.

451
00:32:21,583 --> 00:32:23,375
Tony sir for me and Goofy.
The last option.

452
00:32:23,458 --> 00:32:25,666
-Alka ma'am. Yeah.
-Alka ma'am, sir.

453
00:32:27,375 --> 00:32:28,416
Damn.

454
00:32:29,458 --> 00:32:30,750
All wrong.

455
00:32:30,833 --> 00:32:31,791
Why?

456
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:36,541
I did not always want
to join the Air Force.

457
00:32:39,708 --> 00:32:43,375
Just… Sir, just a sec.
Did you say yes over good coffee?

458
00:32:46,208 --> 00:32:47,333
Yes, buddy.

459
00:32:48,916 --> 00:32:53,416
I thought if someone can make
such good coffee in just a minute,

460
00:32:55,083 --> 00:32:56,791
how much time will she save daily?

461
00:32:57,583 --> 00:32:59,125
How much extra time

462
00:32:59,208 --> 00:33:00,791
we both would have

463
00:33:01,416 --> 00:33:02,625
to live our lives.

464
00:33:04,166 --> 00:33:05,416
I said yes.

465
00:33:05,500 --> 00:33:08,958
Sir, if I may ask, don't take me wrong.

466
00:33:09,666 --> 00:33:12,500
Why did Alka ma'am say yes?
She must've had a reason too.

467
00:33:13,083 --> 00:33:14,000
Just asking.

468
00:33:16,500 --> 00:33:19,541
This you will have to ask
your Alka madam only.

469
00:33:21,708 --> 00:33:23,166
She hasn't told me till date.

470
00:33:24,875 --> 00:33:27,833
-But still, sir, who says yes over coffee?
-Yes, sir, coffee?

471
00:33:58,166 --> 00:34:01,750
Hercules tower, line up runway one-three,
and report ready for departure.

472
00:34:01,833 --> 00:34:03,916
Hercules formation. Cleared to take off.

473
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:05,916
Winds three o'clock. 10 kilometers.

474
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:07,958
Stop time 1.2 kilometers.

475
00:34:08,041 --> 00:34:09,875
Traffic ahead of you. Hyena formation.

476
00:34:09,958 --> 00:34:12,083
Climbing, passing 1.5 kilometers.

477
00:34:32,166 --> 00:34:33,583
0800 IST.

478
00:34:33,666 --> 00:34:34,791
9 Squadron.

479
00:34:34,875 --> 00:34:36,166
-Dash, Nishi.
-Sir!

480
00:34:36,250 --> 00:34:38,083
Hyena 1 and Hyena 2

481
00:34:38,166 --> 00:34:39,916
will drop bombs on Point 4065.

482
00:34:40,625 --> 00:34:44,208
Entering from the eastern heading,
they will exit on the southeast side.

483
00:34:47,666 --> 00:34:49,416
Hyena formation over IP.

484
00:34:49,500 --> 00:34:50,708
We're heading towards the target.

485
00:34:51,291 --> 00:34:53,083
Hyena formation, breaking off.

486
00:34:55,958 --> 00:34:56,791
Ahuja, Dhali.

487
00:34:56,875 --> 00:34:57,708
-Sir!
-Sir!

488
00:34:57,791 --> 00:34:59,500
Hercules 1 and Hercules 2.

489
00:34:59,583 --> 00:35:01,916
You will hold at 55 kilometers southeast.

490
00:35:02,583 --> 00:35:04,166
Upon receiving RT confirmation,

491
00:35:04,250 --> 00:35:06,333
you will cross the target area.

492
00:35:06,416 --> 00:35:09,875
In two minutes, you will cross the target
area and assess bomb damage.

493
00:35:09,958 --> 00:35:11,958
Hercules, standby
for bombing confirmation.

494
00:35:12,041 --> 00:35:14,583
Hercules standing by. Hit them hard, boys.

495
00:35:37,958 --> 00:35:38,791
Captain Waheed.

496
00:35:38,875 --> 00:35:40,458
-Sir.
-Take out the Stinger.

497
00:35:40,541 --> 00:35:42,875
And, everyone else, hide in the sangars!

498
00:35:44,250 --> 00:35:45,208
Yes, sir.

499
00:35:47,833 --> 00:35:49,166
Put it down.

500
00:36:03,708 --> 00:36:05,083
Captain Waheed, hurry up.

501
00:36:05,166 --> 00:36:06,416
I am on it, sir.

502
00:36:10,875 --> 00:36:12,375
What are you doing? Hurry up.

503
00:36:12,458 --> 00:36:14,083
Yes, sir. I'm trying to get a lock.

504
00:36:15,333 --> 00:36:17,083
Hurry up, you will miss them.

505
00:36:18,041 --> 00:36:19,375
Fire!

506
00:36:22,958 --> 00:36:23,916
Oh, shit!

507
00:36:25,458 --> 00:36:28,500
Stinger fire suspected.
Climbing to get out of missile range.

508
00:36:28,583 --> 00:36:29,958
Hyena 1, climb!

509
00:36:38,458 --> 00:36:39,625
How did it miss?

510
00:36:39,708 --> 00:36:42,083
Sir, I fired without getting a lock.

511
00:36:50,250 --> 00:36:51,625
Mayday, mayday, mayday!

512
00:36:51,708 --> 00:36:54,375
Hyena 2, engine flameout. Ejecting!

513
00:37:00,458 --> 00:37:02,083
Rasool, connect to Skardu.

514
00:37:04,583 --> 00:37:05,583
What happened?

515
00:37:05,666 --> 00:37:07,375
Sir, Nishi's jet flamed out.

516
00:37:07,458 --> 00:37:10,000
He was climbing 25,000 feet, sir.
To avoid SAMs.

517
00:37:10,083 --> 00:37:15,375
Sir, an Indian jet has crashed!
On its own, sir.

518
00:37:15,458 --> 00:37:17,416
Ground all jets immediately.

519
00:37:18,708 --> 00:37:21,000
Hercules formation, abort mission.

520
00:37:21,083 --> 00:37:22,208
Abort mission.

521
00:37:22,750 --> 00:37:25,541
Hercules, if you read me,
return to base immediately.

522
00:37:25,625 --> 00:37:26,916
Hostile fire reported in the area.

523
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:28,083
Hyena 2 has ejected.

524
00:37:28,166 --> 00:37:29,083
Copy that.

525
00:37:29,166 --> 00:37:30,500
Khan, did he eject safely?

526
00:37:30,583 --> 00:37:32,416
Negative, we do not have his coordinates.

527
00:37:32,500 --> 00:37:34,458
We're in the same sector.
We'll try to find him.

528
00:37:34,541 --> 00:37:37,041
There are Stingers out there, Hercules.
You have only cameras.

529
00:37:37,125 --> 00:37:38,958
Along with our cameras,
we also have GPS, sir.

530
00:37:39,041 --> 00:37:40,666
We can tell you his exact coordinates.

531
00:37:40,750 --> 00:37:44,291
You do not have any protection.
Return to base immediately.

532
00:37:44,375 --> 00:37:45,750
It is too risky.

533
00:37:46,333 --> 00:37:48,333
-Hyena 1 is returning to base.
-Negative.

534
00:37:48,416 --> 00:37:50,333
We can't return without Hyena 2.

535
00:37:50,416 --> 00:37:51,958
You're deviating
from your planned mission.

536
00:37:52,041 --> 00:37:53,708
Will you please stop
arguing with me, Khan?

537
00:37:53,791 --> 00:37:55,875
I need five minutes. I will find Nishi.

538
00:38:00,916 --> 00:38:02,750
Hercules. Let's do this.

539
00:38:02,833 --> 00:38:04,208
-Fuel check.
-Roger.

540
00:38:04,291 --> 00:38:05,875
Hercules 1. Joker.

541
00:38:05,958 --> 00:38:07,041
I have fuel.

542
00:38:07,125 --> 00:38:08,125
Hercules 2, fuel check.

543
00:38:08,208 --> 00:38:09,375
Hercules 2.

544
00:38:09,458 --> 00:38:10,541
Joker.

545
00:38:10,625 --> 00:38:12,666
Sir, correction, sir.
My needle just jumped.

546
00:38:12,750 --> 00:38:14,041
Be clear, Hercules 2.

547
00:38:14,125 --> 00:38:15,416
Joker or thirsty?

548
00:38:16,291 --> 00:38:17,791
It's thirsty, sir.

549
00:38:17,875 --> 00:38:19,541
Sorry, but my fuel suddenly dipped.

550
00:38:19,625 --> 00:38:21,875
-We have to go back.
-You have to go back.

551
00:38:21,958 --> 00:38:24,708
-Hercules 1, you need to abort as well.
-Negative.

552
00:38:24,791 --> 00:38:28,041
Nishi is alone.
I won't come back until I find him.

553
00:38:28,125 --> 00:38:29,125
Sir, but it's too risky.

554
00:38:29,208 --> 00:38:31,291
You're low on fuel, Hercules 2.

555
00:38:31,916 --> 00:38:33,166
You can be a liability.

556
00:38:33,250 --> 00:38:35,791
But there has to be someone to cover
your tail. It's too risky out there--

557
00:38:35,875 --> 00:38:37,875
That's an order, Hercules 2.

558
00:38:38,416 --> 00:38:39,375
Return to base.

559
00:38:42,416 --> 00:38:43,541
Chin up, soldier.

560
00:38:43,625 --> 00:38:45,291
I'll see you in 20 minutes.

561
00:38:45,375 --> 00:38:46,333
We'll have coffee.

562
00:38:48,375 --> 00:38:49,208
Take care, sir.

563
00:38:51,458 --> 00:38:52,958
Hercules 2, breaking off.

564
00:39:24,875 --> 00:39:26,291
I don't see anything.

565
00:39:27,958 --> 00:39:30,416
I don't have a clear visual.
Need to fly lower.

566
00:39:30,500 --> 00:39:32,083
No, Hercules 1, you can't.

567
00:39:32,166 --> 00:39:34,750
It's too risky.
And you don't have much fuel left.

568
00:39:35,750 --> 00:39:37,541
Enough fuel for one more pass, sir.

569
00:39:39,333 --> 00:39:40,333
I've got this.

570
00:39:59,791 --> 00:40:00,791
Another jet is here!

571
00:40:02,583 --> 00:40:04,000
Reload the SAM again. Hurry!

572
00:40:04,083 --> 00:40:06,000
This time, get a lock and then fire.

573
00:40:12,125 --> 00:40:13,166
It's here.

574
00:40:25,708 --> 00:40:27,375
I have visual. Wreckage spotted.

575
00:40:27,458 --> 00:40:28,500
Khan, stand by for coordinates.

576
00:40:29,833 --> 00:40:30,750
Copy coordinates.

577
00:40:30,833 --> 00:40:33,291
"343833 North,

578
00:40:33,375 --> 00:40:35,666
763524 East."

579
00:40:35,750 --> 00:40:36,875
Roger that, Hercules 1.

580
00:40:36,958 --> 00:40:38,000
Now get the hell out of there.

581
00:40:38,083 --> 00:40:39,416
Roger. Will do that.

582
00:40:42,916 --> 00:40:44,458
-Ready, Captain?
-Yes, sir.

583
00:40:44,541 --> 00:40:46,000
We shouldn't miss this time.

584
00:41:02,791 --> 00:41:04,083
Stinger spotted!

585
00:41:36,750 --> 00:41:38,333
Mayday, mayday, mayday!

586
00:41:38,416 --> 00:41:39,458
Stinger hit!

587
00:41:40,083 --> 00:41:42,250
Roger that, Hercules 1.
We've got you on radar. Call ejecting.

588
00:41:47,583 --> 00:41:51,083
Sir, another Indian jet has crashed!

589
00:41:51,791 --> 00:41:53,500
This time, we shot it down!

590
00:41:58,333 --> 00:41:59,833
Ahuja, can you hear me?

591
00:42:00,375 --> 00:42:01,333
Ahuja, can you hear me?

592
00:42:06,375 --> 00:42:07,458
Losing control.

593
00:42:07,541 --> 00:42:09,083
Looking for valley to eject.

594
00:42:12,041 --> 00:42:15,375
Copy coordinates. "344108 North,

595
00:42:15,458 --> 00:42:17,208
762226 East."

596
00:42:17,291 --> 00:42:18,333
Roger that, Hercules 1.

597
00:42:18,416 --> 00:42:20,291
-Call ejecting.
-Ejecting now!

598
00:46:55,833 --> 00:47:00,833
Subtitle translation by Monika Saraf

